{"parentUuid":"80dc1a55-cd9a-46b9-8fce-06f72d150939","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQLXJe6JSFRoHrn5auUu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing the new Evo component steps (wing final; splitter and arch provisional until their runs finish) in place of the old whole-car and autobahn steps."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4288,"cache_read_input_tokens":287656,"output_tokens":2611,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":272},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4288,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2611,"cache_read_input_tokens":287656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4288,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4288},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f7bee542-25d8-4f01-842d-0a7c47df6359","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011ChQLXJLVHtS669MLgXZ2x","requestRef":"968d657f-4b2d-4b6e-aa08-6a57f05a15d1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"22cc84d3-b5df-432d-9c9e-22f8546b7683","timestamp":"2026-11-25T21:14:06.598Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","madeBy":"model","session_id":"e01a3517-ccd0-4282-af04-8d07c795c5fc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kunabel/workspace/MercedesExperience","sessionId":"5216a6b1-4da7-448e-be48-b0eb888aff5f","version":"2.1.332","gitBranch":"main","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"22cc84d3-b5df-432d-9c9e-22f8546b7683","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQLXJe6JSFRoHrn5auUu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TJVUTD6uhaHu2zBqG5Xbjq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kunabel-workspace-MercedesExperience/5216a6b1-4da7-448e-be48-b0eb888aff5f/scratchpad/evo-comps.js <<'EOF'\n    {\n      id: \"wing\", label: \"Rear wing\", subsystem: \"race-aero\",\n      prompt: \"Watch the orange arrow in the dashed box above the wing's trailing edge. Raise the flap: which way does the air leave the wing now?\",\n      answer: \"Upward. With the flap raised, the mean air direction in the box turns from about 9° down to about 4° up. Turning the air upward takes a push, and the wing feels the push back, downward. In the whole-car model that is about 34 kg more on the rear axle at 200 km/h, for about 9 kW more of the engine's power spent on drag.\",\n      more: \"Wind tunnel details\",\n      view: { pos: [-3.73, 1.88, 1.12], target: [-3.73, 0.238, 1.12] },\n      ghost: { fill: 0, edge: 0 },\n      params: {\n        label: \"Wing flap · a slice of the whole-car tunnel\",\n        data: \"stops/190e-evo2/cfd/wing/\", start: \"base\",\n        // Crop of the whole-car runs (tools/cfd/part.mjs wing; results in tools/cfd/results/wing.json); flap size illustrative.\n        cases: [\n          { id: \"base\", label: \"Baseline\", say: \"Flap down: the air leaves the trailing edge heading slightly downward, about 9° below the horizontal in the box.\" },\n          { id: \"flap\", label: \"Flap raised\", say: \"Flap raised: in the same box the air now rises, about 4° upward, and the paths behind the wing bend up with it.\" },\n        ],\n      },\n      talk: [\n        \"The racing car's rear wing carries an upper flap that teams could raise for circuits with fast bends. Mercedes-Benz names a retractable upper flap and a two-position front spoiler for the homologation car; the flap here is an illustrative size and angle, not the 1992 setting.\",\n        \"The picture is a slice 238 mm from the car's centre line, cut out of a 3-D wind tunnel of the whole car. Colour shows how fast the air moves up (red) or down (blue), as a share of the road speed; grey is solid: the boot lid, the wing and, when raised, the flap.\",\n        \"The orange arrow is the mean direction of the air in the dashed box, over 48 of the model's 28 mm cells. On a coarser 40 mm grid the box holds 12 cells and the direction turns from about 2° down to 6° up: both grids agree on the change, not on its size.\",\n        \"In the whole-car model, raising the flap adds about 34 kg of load on the rear axle at 200 km/h (25 to 43 kg on its two grids) and about 9 kW of drag power (4 to 14 kW); the front axle hardly changes. More rear load is grip and stability in fast bends; the drag is speed lost on the straights.\",\n        \"The model is a game mesh of the Evo II filled with 28 mm blocks: half the car with a mirror on the centre line, a moving road, wheels held still, and a Reynolds number about 300 times smaller than the real car's. Read the change between the two settings, not the values.\",\n      ],\n    },\n    {\n      id: \"splitter\", label: \"Front splitter\", subsystem: \"race-aero\",\n      prompt: \"The lip under the bumper slides forward. Follow the two air paths: one rides up over the nose, one runs under the car. Move the lip forward and watch where they divide.\",\n      answer: \"SPLITTER_ANSWER\",\n      more: \"Wind tunnel details\",\n      view: { pos: [0.84, 1.5, 0.2], target: [0.84, 0, 0.2] },\n      ghost: { fill: 0, edge: 0 },\n      params: {\n        label: \"Front lip · a section through the nose\",\n        data: \"stops/190e-evo2/cfd/splitter/\", start: \"in\",\n        // 2-D section from the traced centre-plane profile (tools/cfd/part.mjs splitter); lip travel and thickness illustrative.\n        cases: [\n          { id: \"in\", label: \"Lip in\", say: \"SPLITTER_IN\" },\n          { id: \"forward\", label: \"Lip forward\", say: \"SPLITTER_FORWARD\" },\n        ],\n      },\n      talk: [\"SPLITTER_TALK\"],\n    },\n    {\n      id: \"wheel-arch\", label: \"Front wheel arch\", subsystem: \"race-aero\",\n      prompt: \"Seen from above at hub height: the bumper corner, the front tyre in its flared arch, the door behind. Tap Follow the air and trace one path from in front of the car.\",\n      answer: \"ARCH_ANSWER\",\n      more: \"Wind tunnel details\",\n      view: { pos: [-0.1, 1.0, 3.6], target: [-0.1, 1.0, 0.34] },\n      ghost: { fill: 0, edge: 0 },\n      params: {\n        label: \"Front corner · seen from above at hub height\",\n        data: \"stops/190e-evo2/cfd/wheel-arch/\", start: \"fitted\", follow: true,\n        // Local 3-D run of the front corner (tools/cfd/part.mjs evo-arch, tools/cfd/corner.mjs).\n        cases: [{ id: \"fitted\", label: \"Flared arch\", say: \"ARCH_SAY\" }],\n      },\n      talk: [\"ARCH_TALK\"],\n    },\nEOF\nnode - <<'EOF'\nconst fs=require(\"fs\"),f=\"stops/190e-evo2/car.js\";let s=fs.readFileSync(f,\"utf8\");\nconst a=s.indexOf('    {\\n      id: \"race-aero\"'), b=s.indexOf('    {\\n      id: \"engine\"');\nif(a<0||b<0)throw new Error(\"anchors\");\ns=s.slice(0,a)+fs.readFileSync(\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kunabel-workspace-MercedesExperience/5216a6b1-4da7-448e-be48-b0eb888aff5f/scratchpad/evo-comps.js\",\"utf8\")+s.slice(b);\nfs.writeFileSync(f,s);\nEOF\ngrep -n 'id: \"' stops/190e-evo2/car.js | head; grep -n \"evo-arch\\|wheel-arch\" tools/cfd/part.mjs | head -3","description":"Replace the Evo's old aero steps with the three part steps"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4288,"cache_read_input_tokens":287656,"output_tokens":2611,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":272},"s