{"parentUuid":"0dd4f5ae-0e46-47c7-adf9-6d780dda1785","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"520f657a-52b6-42e2-ac69-925bae4d884a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Read, Write, mcp__caveman__caveman_retrieve</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user's only message: \"docs/component-cfd-implementation-proposal.md contains fix proposal. Implement it. Update the dev view when done\".\n\n   The proposal asks for the following.\n   - **Evo II:** replace the two whole-car airflow steps (race-aero \"Racing aerodynamics\" and aero \"Road car on the autobahn\") with three component steps: `wing`, `splitter`, `wheel-arch`, then the existing `engine`.\n   - **W 196 R:** replace the 2-D `aero` step with one `wheel` step (enclosed/exposed), then `engine`.\n   - **Data:** offline-computed data per part under `stops/<slug>/cfd/<part>/` (field.json + <case>.bin), produced by `tools/cfd/part.mjs`.\n   - **Player:** a component player in `subsystems/race-aero.js`.\n   - **Copy and tests:** EN/HU copy; unit tests in `lib/model/part-field.js` + `tests/unit/part-field.test.mjs`; e2e covering:\n     - fixed-patch change while paused\n     - A→B→A\n     - re-entry\n     - reduced motion\n     - failure/retry\n     - language replay\n     - offline cold open\n   - **Stop text:** move the Evo road-car figures into its note; put the W196R straight-line estimate in its talk, labelled as a separate calculation.\n   - **Payload:** report package bytes against the old Evo payload of 236,084 B.\n   - **Dev view:** the dev server is already running on :8765 (python, PID 36965). Reload/refresh the user's dev page in Chrome when done.\n\n   Stored memory: Wikimedia photos come via Chrome, with the user's OK.\n\n   Constraints:\n   - Never read or edit `vendor/three/`.\n   - Colours only through CSS tokens.\n   - Panel DOM uses textContent only.\n   - `t(\"literal\")` keys; English source, Hungarian complete.\n   - Commit only if asked (not asked).\n   - The evo2.glb mesh is CC BY-NC and stays local/git-ignored.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Lattice Boltzmann:\n     - 2-D D2Q9 in `lib/model/flow.js` (rasterize, createTunnel; ux + = downstream, rho, cp, single thread ≈16 M cells/s)\n     - 3-D D3Q19 in `tools/cfd/lbm3d.mjs` (createTunnel3d with worker threads; fields() is a cumulative mean; ≈30 M cells/s)\n   - Raw volume layout: 4 Float32 blocks (rho, ui rearward, uj lateral, uk up).\n     - Offset `(k*ny+j)*nx+i`; centre `[x0-(i+.5)h, y0+(j+.5)h, (k+.5)h]`.\n     - `.solid` holds N bytes.\n     - Mirror at y=0.\n   - Part-field format:\n     - Plane \"xz\"/\"xy\"; originMm is the first cell centre; columns decrease x; rows increase z (xz) or y (xy).\n     - Bytes 0..254 quantized over `range`; 255 = solid.\n     - Guides `{kind:\"arrow\"|\"line\", points, faint?, below?}`; optional case `follow:[line idx]`.\n   - Statistics: windowed means (settle 2 flow-throughs, then 3 windows of 1 FT). A result is \"settled\" when the sign repeats on both grids and |d| > 2·se on each.\n   - Reynolds number held fixed across grids by scaling ν.\n     - 2-D: Re 1e4 on 1000 mm, U=0.1.\n     - 3-D: Re 1e4 on the 680 mm tyre diameter, U=0.08.\n   - Tyres are cut flat 48 mm above the road, so clearance is equal on the 24 and 16 mm grids.\n   - three.js rendering: opaque objects render before transparent ones. Overlays must be `transparent:true` so renderOrder puts them above the transparent field quad.\n   - Panel API (lib/app/panel.js):\n     - Buttons: radio via `pressed`, toggles via `toggle:[on,off]`.\n     - `ui.set`, `ui.toggle(id).el`.\n     - state/restore replay.\n     - Widgets marked `detail` go under the step's `more` disclosure.\n   - The caveman MCP compresses large tool outputs. Use `mcp__caveman__caveman_retrieve` with the handle to get full text.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   **tools/cfd/volume.mjs (new)**\n   Side-effect-free reader, shared by the whole-car exporter and the new part exporter.\n   - `load(name, dir=OUT)`:\n     - checks byte counts (16N for the field data, N for the mask)\n     - returns `volume({...meta, rho, ui, uj, uk, solid})`\n   - `volume(r)` adds:\n     - `at`, `centre`, `cell` (nearest, clamped; ny===1 gives j=0)\n     - `vel(x,y,z)`: trilinear, vehicle frame, divided by U; null near a solid. Patched for ny===1 (2-D runs saved as one-row volumes): the j check is skipped and dj=1 is skipped.\n   - `probe(r, box)` → `{n, rearward, lateral, up, angle=atan2(uk,ui)deg}`.\n   - `trace(r, seed, {dt, n, every, plane:\"y\"|\"z\", stop:{x,y,z ranges}})`: RK2, returns rounded mm points.\n\n   **tools/cfd/export.mjs (modified)**\n   - Now imports `{ load as loadRun } from \"./volume.mjs\"`.\n   - `const load = (c, h) => loadRun(`${c}-${h}`, DIR);`\n   - Import of readFileSync removed. Whole-car commands are otherwise unchanged.\n\n   **lib/model/part-field.js (new)**\n   - Exports:\n     - `SOLID=255`, `PLANES`, `QUANTITIES` = [\"vertical-speed-over-inlet\",\"pressure-coefficient\",\"speed-over-inlet\"]\n     - `centre(f,a,b)`\n     - `corners(f)`: outer corners in uv order (0,0), (1,0), (0,1), (1,1)\n     - `quantize`, `dequantize`, `encode(f, sample)`\n     - `decode(f, bytes)`: throws \"field: N bytes, want M\"; returns `{at, solid}`\n     - `problems(f, ids)`: checks plane, quantity, originMm, grid size, range, case ids (order matters), lines, guides, follow\n\n   **tests/unit/part-field.test.mjs (new)**\n   - Fixture tests for orientation, corners and byte format, using an asymmetric 3×2 grid. The xy corner expectation was fixed to `[75,35,30]`.\n   - Per-part test for each race-aero component:\n     - manifest problems\n     - bin sizes\n     - the vertical-speed arrow's dz sign matches the sign of the mean field within 2.5 cells of its tail\n     - `below` lines are slow\n     - for 2+ cases, at least 4 fluid cells change by more than 10% of the scale\n     - asserts `parts.length >= 4`\n   - The first three fixture tests pass. The per-part tests wait for the exports.\n\n   **tools/cfd/corner.mjs (new)**\n   - Exports `GAP=48`, `W196={tyre:{r:340,half:75,y:665},hub:340}`, `EVO={tyre:{r:333,half:135,y:675},hub:333}`.\n   - `lattice(domain,h)`; `DOMAIN` = {\"w196-wheel\": x0 2400 → x1 -2000, Y 1800, Z 1400; \"evo-arch\": x0 1767 → -2000, Y 1800, Z 1600}.\n   - `w196(mode, h, domain=DOMAIN[...])`:\n     - \"enclosed\": streamliner. Half-width 820·sqrt(1-t²) with t=(x-500)/880; top from STREAM_TOP; fender bulge; rounded edges; wheelhouse cavity 40 mm round the tyre and to y<tyre+half+32.\n     - \"exposed\": superellipse body centred at z=450, wy=330s, hz=300s, nose at 950.\n     - Codes: 1 body, 2 tyre.\n   - `evo(mesh, h, domain)`: `voxelize(mesh, L, \"base\")`, then removes the wheels, clips z>1000, carves body cells with y>495 within 378 mm of the hub, adds the tyre.\n   - `sketch(...)`: ASCII slices for checking masks. The masks were inspected and look correct.\n\n   **tools/cfd/part.mjs (new CLI)**\n   - Usage: `node tools/cfd/part.mjs <part> <cmd> [case] [cell mm]`.\n   - Env vars:\n     - `STEPS_SCALE`: quick trials\n     - `TAG`: output dir suffix\n     - `THREADS`\n   - Raw output: `tools/cfd/out/<part>${TAG}/<case>-<h>.{json,bin,solid}`.\n   - Run records: `tools/cfd/results/<part>.json`, written by publish; intended to be checked in.\n   - Settled-change helpers: `change(wa,wb)` and `settled(a,b)`.\n   - **wing:**\n     - WING = box {x[-3920,-3750], y[200,300], z[1230,1290]}, crop {x[-4300,-3150], z[810,1420], y:238}, seeds z [1000,1080,1170,1210,1250,1300,1350,1400] at x=-3180.\n     - `wing reference` writes out/wing/reference.json (probe, changedCells).\n     - `wing export`:\n       - computes crop indices with ceil/floor (41×22, origin [-3171,238,826])\n       - encodes uk/U over range [-0.25,0.25]\n       - traces planar \"y\" paths with dt 6, stopping outside the crop x/z; drops paths that turn back\n       - guides: arrow centred in the box along the probe direction (L=160), a faint box outline, and in base only a faint line where the flap rises (from the flap run's extra cells)\n       - publishes to stops/190e-evo2/cfd/wing/\n   - **splitter (2-D):**\n     - NOSE = [[935,260],[915,440],[870,560],[798,618],[435,674],[48,744]].\n     - SPLIT: cases in/forward, grids [5, 2.5], domain x0 1935 → x1 -665, top 2500; big domain 2935 → -1465, top 3500; edge {in:935, forward:975}; lip z [120,145].\n     - Face samples: upper x[940,970] z[146,162]; lower x[940,970] z[100,118].\n     - Crop x[1335,535], z[0,400]; seeds [[1835,230],[1835,70]].\n     - Section polygon: `[[edge,120],[edge,145],[935,145],...NOSE,[x1-600,744],[x1-600,120]]`.\n     - `splitterSolve(c,h)`:\n       - settle 2 FT, then 3 windows of FT (FT = nx/U·SCALE)\n       - window cp upper/lower/across\n       - saves as a ny=1 volume with y0=-h/2\n       - case \"in-big\" uses the big domain\n     - `splitterExport`:\n       - Cp field on the 5 mm grid (160×80), range [-1,1]\n       - two paths\n       - tick guide line at x=935, z 30→108\n       - record has acrossChange and settled\n   - **corners:**\n     - CORNER[\"w196-wheel\"] = {slug \"w196r\", folder \"wheel\", cases enclosed/exposed, plane 344, station -700, shoulder 740, below 0.8, 8 seeds at x=2200, crop x[1700,-1500], y[0,1500]}.\n     - CORNER[\"evo-arch\"] = {slug \"190e-evo2\", folder \"wheel-arch\", cases [\"fitted\"], plane 344, station -600, seeds at x=1500 with y 700..1100, crop x[1300,-1300], y[0,1400], follow 780}.\n     - grids [24,16]; U 0.08; Re 1e4; D 680.\n     - BIG domains for \"-big\" cases.\n     - `cornerSolve`: settle 2·FT, then 3 windows; window means taken from cumulative `fields()` differences; `observe()` per window.\n     - `observe`:\n       - w196: slow band (speed < 0.8) on the station line nearest the shoulder → {inner, outer, width}\n       - evo: path from (1500, 780, 344) → {y, shift} at the station\n     - `cornerExport`:\n       - xy speed field on 16 mm, range [0,1.4]\n       - planar \"z\" paths\n       - w196 guides: a faint full-station line and the band line with `below`\n       - evo: the follow path is unshifted to index 0 with `follow:[0]`, plus a faint station line\n       - publishes to `stops/<slug>/cfd/<folder>/`\n   - `publish(p, slug, f, bins, rec, folder=p)` validates with problems() and bin sizes, then writes field.json, bins and results/<p>.json.\n\n   **subsystems/race-aero.js (rewritten)**\n   - Params: label, data, cases [{id,label,say}], start, follow.\n   - Field: a single DataTexture with NearestFilter on a quad built from `corners()`.\n   - LUT:\n     - speed: --cfd-1..5 sequential\n     - others: diverging --cfd-2 / --stage / --cfd-5 about zero\n     - solid = --edge, alpha 255; fluid alpha 230\n   - Per-case built groups (cached in `shown` Map):\n     - lines with lineMat (--fg 0.55) or dimMat\n     - cone arrowheads at 0.35/0.7/0.97 of each path\n     - follow tube and start sphere (followMat --accent)\n     - guides: arrow is a rod + cone with markMat --l1; faint lines are dashed; mark lines are rods\n     - particles: DOTS=6 per path\n   - `draw()` applies the whole state once data is in; `say` stays \"\" if `p.follow && !following`.\n   - Drift: clock advances unless paused; speed 0.25 m/s.\n   - Panel main card:\n     - case radio buttons (only if more than 1 case)\n     - follow toggle (`toggle:[t(\"Follow the air\"),t(\"Follow the air\")]`)\n     - pause toggle (`toggle:[t(\"Pause airflow\"),t(\"Pause airflow\")]`, pressed = reducedMotion)\n     - texts \"say\" and \"status\"\n     - \"retry\" button, hidden until a failure\n   - Detail card t(\"Wind tunnel\"): scale svg, plus a legend (--edge \"Solid: the car, cut through\", --fg \"Paths of the mean flow\", --l1 \"The measured air\").\n   - SCALES labels: \"air moving down\"/\"air moving up\"; \"suction\"/\"pressing\"; \"still air\"/\"{0} × road speed\".\n   - `load()`: fetches with HTTP status checks and byte-length checks; on failure shows status t(\"The airflow could not load. Check your connection and try again.\") and unhides retry.\n   - `layout` sets `group.visible = active && !onPhoto`.\n   - Latest fix: markMat and followMat now have `transparent: true` so they draw over the field.\n\n   **stops/190e-evo2/car.js (modified)**\n   - The race-aero and aero components were replaced, via a scratch file, by wing, splitter and wheel-arch, followed by the unchanged engine.\n   - **wing:** final text.\n     - view pos [-3.73,1.88,1.12], target [-3.73,0.238,1.12]; ghost {fill 0, edge 0}; more \"Wind tunnel details\".\n     - params label \"Wing flap · a slice of the whole-car tunnel\", data \"stops/190e-evo2/cfd/wing/\", start \"base\".\n     - cases base \"Baseline\" and flap \"Flap raised\", each with a say.\n     - 5 talk points (crop at y=238; 48/12 cells; 34 kg / 9 kW whole-car figures; model caveats).\n   - **splitter:** view pos [0.84,1.5,0.2], target [0.84,0,0.2] (planned to adjust to ~1.05 distance); data \".../cfd/splitter/\"; start \"in\"; cases in \"Lip in\" / forward \"Lip forward\".\n   - **wheel-arch:** view pos [-0.1,1.0,3.6], target [-0.1,1.0,0.34]; data \".../cfd/wheel-arch/\"; start \"fitted\"; follow true; case fitted \"Flared arch\".\n     - Better planned view: pos [0,1.3,3.5], target [0,0.75,0.344] (camera on +y side, so downstream is screen right).\n   - Placeholders still to replace: SPLITTER_ANSWER, SPLITTER_IN, SPLITTER_FORWARD, SPLITTER_TALK, ARCH_ANSWER, ARCH_SAY, ARCH_TALK.\n   - Still to update: lede, note (add the road-car figures: Cd 0.29 vs 0.32, 235 hp, ~250 km/h), unverified (remove the road-car wind-tunnel and 3-D lines; add wing/splitter/arch lines), and possibly add the MDPI source.\n\n   **stops/w196r/car.js (modified)**\n   - The aero component was replaced with `wheel`:\n     - view pos [0.1,1.3,4.1], target [0.1,0.75,0.344]; ghost 0; more \"Wind tunnel details\"\n     - label \"Front corner · seen from above at hub height\"; data \"stops/w196r/cfd/wheel/\"; start \"enclosed\"\n     - cases Enclosed/Exposed\n   - Placeholders: WHEEL_ANSWER, WHEEL_ENCLOSED, WHEEL_EXPOSED, WHEEL_TALK.\n   - Still to update:\n     - lede (\"Switch bodies and see what the cover is worth...\" → about watching the air behind the wheel)\n     - talk: history, the Silverstone corner trade-off, and the separate straight-line estimate (\"about 20 km/h faster at 290 hp in a separate calculation with assumed drag figures\")\n     - unverified: remove the centre-plane and 2-D lines; add the local 3-D line with assumed body/tyre sizes\n   - The user's in-progress engine component was preserved.\n\n   **lib/app/viewer.js / lib/app/story.js (modified)**\n   - Added `project(p mm) → [cssX, cssY]` in viewer, exposed in the story debug handle as `project: p => s.viewer?.project(p)`.\n\n   **lib/app/i18n/hu.js (modified)**\n   - Removed: \"1.6 × road speed\", \"Extra drag\", \"Extra load on the axle\", \"Front axle\", \"Rear axle\", \"Streamlines of the mean flow\", \"The changed part\", \"kg\".\n   - Added:\n     - \"{0} × road speed\": \"a menetsebesség {0}-szerese\"\n     - \"air moving down\": \"lefelé áramló levegő\"\n     - \"air moving up\": \"felfelé áramló levegő\"\n     - \"Follow the air\": \"Kövesse a levegőt\"\n     - \"Pause airflow\": \"Áramlás megállítása\"\n     - \"Loading the airflow…\": \"Az áramlás betöltése…\"\n     - \"Try again\": \"Próbálja újra\"\n     - \"The airflow could not load. Check your connection and try again.\": \"Az áramlást nem sikerült betölteni. Ellenőrizze a kapcsolatot, és próbálja újra.\"\n     - \"Solid: the car, cut through\": \"Tömör: az autó metszete\"\n     - \"Paths of the mean flow\": \"Az átlagos áramlás útvonalai\"\n     - \"The measured air\": \"A mért levegő\"\n   - The catalog tests now pass. Only the stops' hu.js tests fail.\n\n   **tests/e2e/smoke.spec.mjs (modified)**\n   - race-aero steps call `precomputed(step, comp)` and `continue`; other subsystems keep the readout assertion.\n\n   **tests/e2e/helpers.mjs (modified)**\n   - Imports expect.\n   - Added `precomputed(step, comp)`:\n     - follow parts: click \"Follow the air\", expect pressed, expect say == cases[0].say\n     - otherwise: expect the start say, click the other case, expect it pressed and its say\n\n   **tests/e2e/part-flow.spec.mjs (new)**\n   - Paused fixed-patch screenshot-clip change for Evo wing at point [-4060,238,1340] and for w196r wheel at [-1100,900,344]. The w196r point may need adjusting after results.\n   - Quick A→B→A with delayed bins, re-entry, and language replay (Hungarian flap label \"Szárnylap fent\" assumed to remain in hu.js).\n   - Failure/retry on splitter bins.\n   - Reduced motion on wheel-arch.\n\n   **tests/e2e/offline.spec.mjs (modified)**\n   - After going offline, cold-opens 190e-evo2 and w196r and runs `precomputed` on each race-aero step.\n\n   **Other files**\n   - `tools/cfd/out/logs/run3d.sh` (git-ignored) runs these sequentially with THREADS=7:\n     - w196 enclosed 24, exposed 24, evo fitted 24\n     - w196 enclosed 16, exposed 16, evo fitted 16\n     - w196 exposed-big 24\n   - Logs are in tools/cfd/out/logs/ (3d.log, split-5.log, split-in-2.5.log, split-fwd-2.5.log).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Wing crop was 42×23 instead of 41×22:** nearest-cell rounding took a cell outside the range. Fixed with ceil/floor bounds so only centres inside the crop count.\n   - **Test expectation wrong:** the corners(xy)[3] y value was corrected from 40 to 35.\n   - **Leftover `};` after the load refactor in export.mjs:** removed with perl.\n   - **volume.vel returned null for ny=1 (2-D) runs:** patched.\n   - **Arrow and guides hidden under the transparent field quad** (opaque pass renders before transparent): made the overlay materials transparent.\n   - **Wing paths started outside the crop and curled back through the separated boot flow:** reseeded at x=-3180, added stop bounds, and filtered out paths that turn back.\n   - **stop-shot 404s:** the wheel-arch data is not exported yet. Expected.\n   - **Bash `--include=*.js` failed in zsh** (no match glob): avoided.\n   - **No PIL available** for stacking images.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Reproduced the proposal's numbers exactly:\n     - probe 48/12 cells\n     - angles −8.6→4.0 (28 mm) and −2.3→5.7 (40 mm)\n     - changed cells 90/39\n   - Evo mesh flare: max |y| ≈ 800, while the tyre's outer face is at 810. No slimmer arch can clear the tyre, so the arch ships as a single-state \"Follow the air\" lesson, as the proposal permits.\n   - Timings:\n     - 2-D 5 mm (260k cells) ≈ 13–23 ms/step\n     - 2.5 mm ≈ 56–90 ms/step, so roughly 60–80 min per case\n     - 3-D 24 mm (0.8M cells) ≈ 26 ms/step at 10 threads\n     - 16 mm runs ≈ 30–40 min each\n     - Solves started around 22:11, at 7 threads plus 3 splitter processes\n   - A quick 24 mm exposed trial gave a wake band of about 586–770 (width 130–180), which looks plausible.\n   - Wing visual (latest capture): orange arrow clearly visible, paths cleaner. The flap case shows the arrow tipping slightly up and the raised flap cells. Base case still to recheck.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"docs/component-cfd-implementation-proposal.md contains fix proposal. Implement it. Update the dev view when done\"\n   - No other user messages apart from system \"say what you're doing\" nudges.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Wait for the background solves, then run `node tools/cfd/part.mjs splitter export`, `w196-wheel export` and `evo-arch export`. Check the records (settled flags, band widths, path shifts) and the big-domain sensitivity.\n   - Replace all placeholder texts (SPLITTER_*, ARCH_*, WHEEL_*) with captions based on the computed results.\n     - Splitter: if the face-pressure change is not settled, describe the two paths and how the lip divides the