{"parentUuid":"015bb904-bcad-4a52-9515-49bd58f749d8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"520f657a-52b6-42e2-ac69-925bae4d884a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LEn2enonHmcy24PiruLAVt","type":"tool_result","content":"139:- Wind-tunnel sections: Blitzen-Benz and 190 E Evo II are traced (the Evo II from its stop photo, a side view; rear wing\n140-  left out). Approximate: W 196 R, 540 K Cabriolet B and Blue Wonder (ghost outlines plus a few centre-line points on 3/4\n141-  photos); sketched: the 540 K Streamliner, the racing car on the Blue Wonder's deck and the boxy truck. A side photo per\n142-  the recipe would firm them up.\n143:- Evo II 3-D wind tunnel (race-aero, tools/cfd): for understanding, not engineering. Simplified voxel model (game mesh as\n144-  28 mm blocks, half car mirrored, flat floor, still wheels, Reynolds number ~3 × 10⁴ vs 10⁷), forces from mean surface\n145-  pressure only (no friction). The stop shows the mean of the 28 and 40 mm grids, and only changes with the same sign on both\n146-  whose mean clears the pooled scatter: the flap's drag, lift and rear load are settled (front load is not); nothing of the lip is\n147-  (both grids: a little less downforce, no clear front gain); the arch trim is finer than a cell, its solid equals the\n148-  baseline's, and export.mjs leaves it out. A finer grid or longer averaging would be needed to say more.\n149-- Not added from docs/research.md: the Vision R 320 CDI (its exhibition has ended) and the Vision Mercedes-Maybach 6\n150-  (never shown at the museum).\n151-- The original single-file PoC pages are in git history at commit 468cc29 (`museum-tour-poc/`).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ae7f0b44-5596-4fb9-b852-1256d06bb811","timestamp":"2026-11-25T22:16:34.410Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"139:- Wind-tunnel sections: Blitzen-Benz and 190 E Evo II are traced (the Evo II from its stop photo, a side view; rear wing\n140-  left out). Approximate: W 196 R, 540 K Cabriolet B a