{"parentUuid":"9e83c725-f40a-4d30-8eba-717001b75c4a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"520f657a-52b6-42e2-ac69-925bae4d884a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EYfQbGBBtxg3HQzjqHxYH6","type":"tool_result","content":"142:- Airflow close-ups (race-aero; Evo II wing, splitter, wheel arch; W 196 R front wheel): for understanding, not engineering.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0548f6ed-3629-4286-b930-95d801e10fcb","timestamp":"2026-11-25T22:16:45.937Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"142:- Airflow close-ups (race-aero; Evo II wing, splitter, wheel arch; W 196 R front wheel): for understanding, not engineering.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kunabel/workspace/MercedesExperience/CLAUDE.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":136,"oldLines":16,"newStart":136,"newLines":18,"lines":["   Flickr photos only). The Ponton stop shows a 1955 180 (research names the 220); the R 129 of Legend 6 is told with Princess","   Diana's 500 SL; the 540 K Streamliner is the existing 540k stop. Illustrative throughout: LP 333 axle spacings, Unimog","   portal sizes, O 302 heat balance, 600 hydraulic sizes, ABS and rollover parameters (each car.js `unverified`).","-- Wind-tunnel sections: Blitzen-Benz and 190 E Evo II are traced (the Evo II from its stop photo, a side view; rear wing","-  left out). Approximate: W 196 R, 540 K Cabriolet B and Blue Wonder (ghost outlines plus a few centre-line points on 3/4","-  photos); sketched: the 540 K Streamliner, the racing car on the Blue Wonder's deck and the boxy truck. A side photo per","-  the recipe would firm them up.","-- Evo II 3-D wind tunnel (race-aero, tools/cfd): for understanding, not engineering. Simplified voxel model (game mesh as","-  28 mm blocks, half car mirrored, flat floor, still wheels, Reynolds number ~3 × 10⁴ vs 10⁷), forces from mean surface","-  pressure only (no friction). The stop shows the mean of the 28 and 40 mm grids, and only changes with the same sign on both","-  whose mean clears the pooled scatter: the flap's drag, lift and rear load are settled (front load is not); nothing of the lip is","-  (both grids: a little less downforce, no clear front gain); the arch trim is finer than a cell, its solid equals the","-  baseline's, and export.mjs leaves it out. A finer grid or longer averaging would be needed to say more.","+- Wind-tunnel sections: Blitzen-Benz is traced. Approximate: 540 K Cabriolet B and Blue Wonder (ghost outlines plus a few","+  centre-line points on 3/4 photos); sketched: the 540 K Streamliner, the racing car on the Blue Wonder's deck and the boxy","+  truck. A side photo per the recipe would firm them up.","+- Airflow close-ups (race-aero; Evo II wing, splitter, wheel arch; W 196 R front wheel): for understanding, not engineering.","+  Each runs on two grids and tools/cfd/results/<part>.json records the windows and whether a change is settled (same sign","+  on both grids, above twice its scatter and the case's drift). Wing: a crop of the archived 28 mm whole-car run (game mesh","+  as blocks, half car mirrored, flat floor, still wheels, Reynolds number ~3 × 10⁴ vs 10⁷): the flap turns the air upward on","+  both grids, by different amounts; flap size and angle illustrative. No local wing solve with a sampled inlet yet.","+  Splitter: 2-D nose section, lip travel and thickness illustrative. Corners: local 3-D tunnels (corner.mjs), tyre still,","+  48 mm above the road, Reynolds number 10⁴ on the tyre; W 196 R body shapes simplified from the outline; the Evo flare","+  already sits at the tyre's outer face, so the arch has one state and no comparison. The whole-car Evo forces","+  (export.mjs) are no longer shown: the 34 kg / 9 kW flap figures in the wing step come from them."," - Not added from docs/research.md: the Vision R 320 CDI (its exhibition has ended) and the Vision Mercedes-Maybach 6","   (never shown at the museum)."," - The original single-file PoC pages are in git history at commit 468cc29 (`museum-tour-poc/`)."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kunabel/workspace/MercedesExperience/CLAUDE.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8b4b87cf-493d-420a-85dd-8fd06347244e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/kunabel/workspace/MercedesExperience","root":"/Users/kunabel/workspace/MercedesExperience","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"abelkun-androniq/MercedesExperience","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"abelkun-androniq/MercedesExperience","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"abelkun-androniq/MercedesExperience","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/kunabel/workspace/MercedesExperience","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9e83c725-f40a-4d30-8eba-717001b75c4a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"e01a3517-ccd0-4282-af04-8d07c795c5fc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kunabel/workspace/MercedesExperience","sessionId":"5216a6b1-4da7-448e-be48-b0eb888aff5f","version":"2.1.332","gitBranch":"main","slug":"snoopy-wiggling-shell-of-5216a6b1-4da7-448e-be48-b0eb888aff5f","dataFlowOn":true}
