{"attachment":{"command":"","content":"","durationMs":32,"exitCode":0,"hookEvent":"","hookName":"","stderr":"","stdout":"","toolUseID":"","type":"hook_success"},"cwd":"/Users/kunabel/workspace/MercedesExperience","dataFlowOn":true,"entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"parentUuid":"b0c536f5-2731-49ac-9b50-063f7a7df06e","sessionId":"5216a6b1-4da7-448e-be48-b0eb888aff5f","session_id":"e01a3517-ccd0-4282-af04-8d07c795c5fc","slug":"snoopy-wiggling-shell-of-5216a6b1-4da7-448e-be48-b0eb888aff5f","timestamp":"2026-11-25T22:38:06.931Z","type":"attachment","userType":"external","uuid":"aef27cdb-21ea-46f8-b56a-d31d4d604bbc","version":"2.1.332"}
{"parentUuid":"b0c536f5-2731-49ac-9b50-063f7a7df06e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"520f657a-52b6-42e2-ac69-925bae4d884a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E1ouma3o2UpwUaHUMVc7zR","type":"tool_result","content":"**Splitter.** Draw two closed nose sections from the same bumper profile and ride height. Extend the lip longitudinally. The current 40 mm travel and 25 mm thickness are illustrative. Start at 5 mm per cell, which gives eight cells of travel and five through the plate, then repeat at finer spacing, for example 2.5 mm. Use `rasterize()` and `createTunnel()` from the existing 2-D model in Node. Allow fluid above and below the lip and continue the underside past the visible crop. Keep the road moving and the local domain larger than the on-screen view. Fix the model Reynolds number across refinements by scaling lattice viscosity with the feature length in cells at the same lattice inlet speed. Sample `cp(c)` on fluid cells beside each face over a stated chord interval and average over settled steps. Trace the two paths from fixed inlet seeds in the mean velocity field. Put the pressure map and old-edge tick in the export. If the face-pressure *change between settings* falls inside the variation, keep the position toggle and describe the visible upper/lower paths. Omit a front-axle load estimate. [Live solver functions](../lib/model/flow.js) · [Lip geometry](../tools/cfd/geometry.mjs)\n\n### D. Compute the two front-wheel experiments\n    // Reference pressure p∞: the oncoming air a few cells behind the inlet (drag builds a pressure drop along the tunnel, so\n    // the inlet's own density is not the free stream's).\n    let s = 0, n = 0; for (let j = 0; j < nz; j++) if (!solid[j * nx + 3]) { s += rho[j * nx + 3]; n++; }\n    ref = s / n;\n    drag.total = fx; drag.push = (rf - nf * ref) / 3; drag.suction = -(rr - nr * ref) / 3; drag.friction = fx - drag.push - drag.suction;\n  }\n\n  // Pressure coefficient (p − p∞) / ½ρU² at cell c: lattice pressure is ρ/3.\n  let ref = 1;\n  const cp = c => (rho[c] - ref) / 3 / (0.5 * U * U);\n  // Bilinear velocity at fractional cell coordinates (cell centres at integers), for tracer particles. Solid cells read 0.\n  function sample(x, z, out) {\n    const i = Math.max(0, Math.min(nx - 1.001, x)), j = Math.max(0, Math.min(nz - 1.001, z)), i0 = i | 0, j0 = j | 0, a = i - i0, b = j - j0;\n    const c = j0 * nx + i0, w00 = (1 - a) * (1 - b), w10 = a * (1 - b), w01 = (1 - a) * b, w11 = a * b;\n    out[0] = w00 * ux[c] + w10 * ux[c + 1] + w01 * ux[c + nx] + w11 * ux[c + nx + 1];\n    out[1] = w00 * uz[c] + w10 * uz[c + 1] + w01 * uz[c + nx] + w11 * uz[c + nx + 1];\n    return out;\n  }\n  return { nx, nz, U, solid, ux, uz, rho, drag, step, cp, sample };\n}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"236e7082-91bb-43de-868e-863d32bcb794","timestamp":"2026-11-25T22:38:07.547Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"**Splitter.** Draw two closed nose sections from the same bumper profile and ride height. Extend the lip longitudinally. The current 40 mm travel and 25 mm thickness are illustrative. Start at 5 mm per cell, which gives eight cells of travel and five through the plate, then repeat at finer spacing, for example 2.5 mm. Use `rasterize()` and `createTunnel()` from the existing 2-D model in Node. Allow fluid above and below the lip and continue the underside past the visible crop. Keep the road moving and the local domain larger than the on-screen view. Fix the model Reynolds number across refinements by scaling lattice viscosity with the feature length in cells at the same lattice inlet speed. Sample `cp(c)` on fluid cells beside each face over a stated chord interval and average over settled steps. Trace the two paths from fixed inlet seeds in the mean velocity field. Put the pressure map and old-edge tick in the export. If the face-pressure *change between settings* falls inside the variation, keep the position toggle and describe the visible upper/lower paths. Omit a front-axle load estimate. [Live solver functions](../lib/model/flow.js) · [Lip geometry](../tools/cfd/geometry.mjs)\n\n### D. Compute the two front-wheel experiments\n    // Reference pressure p∞: the oncoming air a few cells behind the inlet (drag builds a pressure drop along the tunnel, so\n    // the inlet's own density is not the free stream's).\n    let s = 0, n = 0; for (let j = 0; j < nz; j++) if (!solid[j * nx + 3]) { s += rho[j * nx + 3]; n++; }\n    ref = s / n;\n    drag.total = fx; drag.push = (rf - nf * ref) / 3; drag.suction = -(rr - nr * ref) / 3; drag.friction = fx - drag.push - drag.suction;\n  }\n\n  // Pressure coefficient (p − p∞) / ½ρU² at cell c: lattice pressure is ρ/3.\n  let ref = 1;\n  const cp = c => (rho[c] - ref) / 3 / (0.5 * U * U);\n  // Bilinear velocity at fractional cell coordinates (cell centres at integers), for tracer particles. Solid cells read 0.\n  function sample(x, z, out) {\n    const i = Math.max(0, Math.min(nx - 1.001, x)), j = Math.max(0, Math.min(nz - 1.001, z)), i0 = i | 0, j0 = j | 0, a = i - i0, b = j - j0;\n    const c = j0 * nx + i0, w00 = (1 - a) * (1 - b), w10 = a * (1 - b), w01 = (1 - a) * b, w11 = a * b;\n    out[0] = w00 * ux[c] + w10 * ux[c + 1] + w01 * ux[c + nx] + w11 * ux[c + nx + 1];\n    out[1] = w00 * uz[c] + w10 * uz[c + 1] + w01 * uz[c + nx] + w11 * uz[c + nx + 1];\n    return out;\n  }\n  return { nx, nz, U, solid, ux, uz, rho, drag, step, cp, sample };\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"33d2c232-a45a-4f37-8468-aa1c3ac36dc1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/kunabel/workspace/MercedesExperience","root":"/Users/kunabel/workspace/MercedesExperience","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"abelkun-androniq/MercedesExperience","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"abelkun-androniq/MercedesEx