{"parentUuid":"851930bf-11df-4b34-b878-72ee686f6ac7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQTR3ioizX6LHuApxMy4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've done most of the proposal, but the stops aren't finished. Three steps still have number placeholders in their text, waiting on the fine-grid runs. The dev view isn't refreshed yet, because those runs are still going.\n\n**What's done:**\n- **Evo II:** the two whole-car airflow steps are replaced by wing → splitter → wheel arch, then the existing engine.\n- **W 196 R:** the old `aero` step is replaced by a front-wheel step (enclosed / exposed).\n- **Viewer:** each step shows a computed field, air paths, case buttons, Follow the air and Pause airflow, with a \"Try again\" button if the data fails to load.\n- **Text:** English and Hungarian are written for all four steps. The Evo road-car figures (Cd 0.29 against 0.32, 235 hp, about 250 km/h) are now in its note. The W 196 R straight-line estimate is in its talk, labelled as a separate calculation with assumed figures.\n- **Old files:** the whole-car display files are removed from the stop; `export.mjs` now writes them to the git-ignored `tools/cfd/out/whole-car/`. CLAUDE.md is updated.\n- **Payload:** about 91 kB for both stops (Evo 55 kB), against the old 236,084 B.\n\n**Tests:**\n- Unit tests: 240 pass. The one failure is the Evo config check on the splitter text, which I've since written but haven't re-run.\n- The five new part-flow browser tests pass on iPhone. The full `npm run e2e` hasn't been run yet.\n\n**Results so far (coarse grid unless noted):**\n- **Wing:** with the flap raised, the air over the wing's trailing edge turns from about 9° down to about 4° up. The 40 mm grid agrees on the direction but not the size.\n- **W 196 R wheel:** behind the exposed tyre there's a band of slow air about 23 cm wide (24 mm grid). With the wheel enclosed, only a layer about 4 cm thick stays slow along the body skin (24 mm grid), and about 3 cm on the 16 mm grid.\n- **Evo arch:** the followed path is pushed about 38 cm outward by the bumper corner and flare. It has one state only, because the mesh's flare already sits at the tyre's outer face, so there's no narrower arch to compare.\n- **Splitter (5 mm grid only):** with the lip forward, the pressure difference across the lip's front end is larger in every averaging window. But the flow under the car was still settling, so its size kept shrinking; the text gives the direction only, no load.\n\n**Where I departed from the proposal:**\n- **Splitter shading:** it shows air speed, not pressure. In this 2-D model the whole tunnel's pressure level drifts, so absolute pressure readings would mislead. The lip comparison uses the pressure difference across the lip, which isn't affected.\n- **Splitter domain:** I first tried opening the underside behind the bumper so the underbody flow would settle faster. That made the solver blow up, so I reverted to the closed underside. It now settles for three flow-throughs, and the settled check also requires the change to beat each case's drift between windows.\n- **Wing:** it's still a slice of the archived whole-car run. The local wing solve the proposal describes isn't implemented; the step and its notes say so.\n\n**Still running:** the W 196 R exposed and Evo arch runs at 16 mm, the splitter at 2.5 mm, and two larger-domain sensitivity runs. The 2.5 mm splitter runs are the slow ones, roughly two hours. When they finish I'll fill in the remaining numbers in both languages, then run `npm test` and the full `npm run e2e`. Last, I'll reload your localhost:8765 page in Chrome."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":761,"cache_read_input_tokens":202068,"output_tokens":1274,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":16},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},