{"parentUuid":"0637c3d7-c52f-4d90-a781-2c5fa5feae8e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQTSKuvYoVruxoDzUUEj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The work is mostly done. What's left is waiting for the last simulations to finish, and three steps still have number placeholders in their text until then.\n\n**Where each step stands:**\n\n| Step | Picture | Text | Waiting on |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Evo rear wing | Final | Final, EN + HU | Nothing |\n| Evo front splitter | Preview from the 5 mm grid | Written | The 2.5 mm runs, about 2 h more |\n| Evo wheel arch | Preview from the 24 mm grid | Written; shift and grid note missing | The 16 mm run, after the W 196 R one |\n| W 196 R front wheel | Preview from the 24 mm grid | Written; wake widths and grid note missing | The exposed 16 mm run, now going |\n\nThe five new browser tests pass on iPhone, and the Evo and W 196 R pages load without errors.\n\n**What's causing problems:**\n\n1. **Run time.** Each part has to run on two grids, and the fine grids are slow. The machine is also oversubscribed: four splitter processes plus a seven-thread 3-D solver on 10 cores. At this rate the 3-D runs finish around 01:00 and the 2.5 mm splitter runs around 02:00.\n2. **The splitter model is weak, and that cost a restart.**\n   - The air channel under the car takes a long time to settle, so the pressure under the lip kept drifting through every averaging window.\n   - My fix for that (opening up the underside behind the bumper) made the solver blow up, which threw away about 20 minutes of runs. I went back to the original shape and lengthened the settling instead.\n   - Pressure can't be shown as a picture: in this 2-D model the whole tunnel's pressure level drifts, so absolute readings mean nothing. The splitter now shows air speed instead. The lip comparison uses the pressure difference across the lip, which isn't affected.\n   - Even so, the result is only directional. Pushing the lip forward increases the difference in every window, but its size kept shrinking, so the text gives no number.\n3. **The Evo arch has nothing to compare.** The game mesh's flared arch already sits right at the tyre's outer edge, so a narrower arch would leave the tyre uncovered. The arch step therefore shows one state and traces where the air goes, rather than an arch on/off switch.\n4. **The wing still uses the old whole-car run.** The proposal's local wing simulation isn't implemented. The wing step shows a slice of the earlier whole-car run, and the notes say so.\n\n**To finish sooner:** I could stop the 2.5 mm splitter runs. The splitter would then ship on the 5 mm grid alone, and its notes would say it was checked on one grid only. That would bring completion to about 01:00. Otherwise I'll wait for all runs, then fill in the numbers in both languages, run the full tests and reload your page."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":765,"cache_read_input_tokens":204119,"output_tokens":1110,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":157},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":765,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1110,"cache_read_input_tokens":204119,"cache_creation_input_tokens":765,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":765},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.4.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.4.content.1","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.6.content.0"