{"parentUuid":"20fdc960-d1b8-4f70-af32-3f3293e8096b","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"turn_duration","durationMs":45621,"messageCount":812,"timestamp":"2026-11-25T22:54:22.431Z","uuid":"f92f457e-1570-422b-9d3c-6b0465faa837","isMeta":false,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kunabel/workspace/MercedesExperience","sessionId":"5216a6b1-4da7-448e-be48-b0eb888aff5f","version":"2.1.332","gitBranch":"main","slug":"snoopy-wiggling-shell-of-5216a6b1-4da7-448e-be48-b0eb888aff5f","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"f92f457e-1570-422b-9d3c-6b0465faa837","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"away_summary","content":"Goal: ship the four airflow close-ups for the Evo II and W 196 R. Two Chrome tabs show provisional results for you to check. Next: when the fine-grid runs finish, add their final numbers in English and Hungarian, run the full tests, and reload both tabs.","timestamp":"2026-11-25T22:57:24.612Z","uuid":"a6ed87f1-f9e8-4c01-abeb-7ac63337e378","isMeta":false,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kunabel/workspace/MercedesExperience","sessionId":"5216a6b1-4da7-448e-be48-b0eb888aff5f","version":"2.1.332","gitBranch":"main","slug":"snoopy-wiggling-shell-of-5216a6b1-4da7-448e-be48-b0eb888aff5f","dataFlowOn":true}
{"parentUuid":"a6ed87f1-f9e8-4c01-abeb-7ac63337e378","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4f944dac-45da-479e-aa7a-6e08919bf481","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"I asked for an expert review. Here it is: \n\n<pasted_content id=\"ccbe\">\nReply plan for the drafting model — Aim for 400 words. Use the findings below. No new simulations are needed to draft the reply.\n\n1. Open with four verdicts.\n   - Wing — yes, for the recorded local direction change. Raising the flap increased the mean angle in the marked box by +12.6° and +8.0° on the two grids. Nearby probes retain the positive change, but the absolute down-to-up reversal depends on placement. Prefer collecting local angle histories before funding a nested solve.\n   - Splitter — no load sign. Both probes cover x=940–970 mm. The retracted lip ends at 935 mm, so both probes sample free fluid in that case. Longer averaging cannot repair this comparison.\n   - W 196 R — no two-grid sign yet. 574–806 mm are edge coordinates. The coarse mean-field widths are 232 mm exposed and 40 mm enclosed. The enclosed band starts at the first interpolable fluid point. The fine exposed case and paired larger-domain check are missing.\n   - Evo arch — yes as a single-state illustration. The projected mean streamline bends outward about 0.37 m. Avoid attributing the displacement to the flare or presenting the line as a particle trajectory.\n2. Give the minimum splitter repair. Specify a velocity inlet with reconstructed density and a remote static-pressure outlet with reconstructed normal velocity. Use a uniform upstream patch for Cₚ. A sponge addresses reflections. A uniform pressure offset cancels across the lip, and idealized gap relaxation takes about 5.6 current tunnel transits. Leave the drift’s cause open until mass, gap flux and force histories settle. Integrate vertical pressure force on actual wetted faces.\n3. Make domain adequacy testable. Prefer a finite section whose upper and lower flows rejoin before the outlet. A truncated section needs downstream pressures or resistance from a credible parent model. Current solid blockage is 25%. Enlarge the coarse domain for both settings and compare the case contrasts. No universal inlet distance or ceiling height guarantees the sign.\n4. End with the release gate and budget. Hold physical geometry, molecular Re, low Mach and probe location fixed. Grid-tied Smagorinsky refinement tests model sensitivity. Check tyre gap, rotation and confinement separately. Prefer integrated axial deficit over a common fluid patch to a two-cell threshold width. After a coarse pilot, use decorrelated batches and require each grid’s 95% contrast interval to lie on the same side of zero, with domain sensitivity smaller than the credible effect. Six fine splitter transits per case already cost roughly 2.25 machine-hours for the pair. If the budget expires first, mark the sign unresolved.\n\nUse the existing boundary notes (research_notes/Museum airflow claim review/section.md), exhibit measurements (research_notes/Museum airflow claim review/parts.md) and statistical protocol (research_notes/Museum airflow claim review/statistics.md) for sources.\n</pasted_content id=\"ccbe\">\n\n what does that tell you?"},"uuid":"da0c676b-86a5-42a0-868e-c1216b13541d","timestamp":"2026-11-25T23:00:33.261Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","turnOrigin":"human","turnPromptId":"4f944dac-45da-479e-aa7a-6e08919bf481","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":6,"turnIndex":6},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kunabel/workspace/MercedesExperience","sessionId":"5216a6b1-4da7-448e-be48-b0eb888aff5f","version":"2.1.332","gitBranch":"main","slug":"snoopy-wiggling-shell-of-5216a6b1-4da7-448e-be48-b0eb888aff5f","dataFlowOn":true}
