st stream outside (red).\",","       more: \"Wind tunnel details\",","       view: { pos: [0, 1.3, 3.8], target: [0, 0.75, 0.344] },","       ghost: { fill: 0, edge: 0 },"]},{"oldStart":89,"oldLines":13,"newStart":89,"newLines":13,"lines":["         label: \"Front corner · seen from above at hub height\",","         data: \"stops/190e-evo2/cfd/wheel-arch/\", start: \"fitted\", follow: true,","         // Local 3-D run of the front corner (tools/cfd/part.mjs evo-arch, tools/cfd/corner.mjs).","-        cases: [{ id: \"fitted\", label: \"Flared arch\", say: \"This path starts in line with the tyre, just in front of the bumper corner. The corner and the flared arch push it about 38 cm outward; it keeps that line past the door.\" }],","+        cases: [{ id: \"fitted\", label: \"Flared arch\", say: \"This path of the mean flow starts in line with the tyre, just in front of the bumper corner. The car's front corner turns it about 38 cm outward, and it keeps that line past the door.\" }],","       },","       talk: [","         \"The Evolution II's arches were widened so that wider wheels and tyres would fit under the body, and shaped with the rest of the body kit in the wind tunnel.\",","-        \"The picture is a level slice at hub height through a 3-D wind tunnel of the front corner, computed ahead of time from the same game mesh as the rear wing. Colour is the air's speed against the road speed; grey is solid, body and tyre cut through.\",","+        \"The picture is a level slice at hub height through a 3-D wind tunnel of the front corner, computed ahead of time from the same game mesh as the rear wing. Colour is the air's speed against the road speed; grey is solid, body and tyre cut through. The blue line follows the time-averaged flow in this level slice; a single puff of air wanders around it with the turbulence.\",","         \"The tyre stands still in its carved-out wheelhouse, 48 mm above a moving road; the body is cut flat 1 m up and the half car is mirrored 