s simplified from the outline; the Evo flare","-  already sits at the tyre's outer face, so the arch has one state and no comparison. The whole-car Evo forces","-  (export.mjs) are no longer shown: the 34 kg / 9 kW flap figures in the wing step come from them.","+  An expert review (research_notes/Museum airflow claim review/) set the rules: claim a sign only when, per grid, the 95 %","+  interval over one-flow-through batches lies on one side of zero, the same side on both grids, and a larger tunnel moves","+  it less than the effect (`gate` in part.mjs; records in tools/cfd/results/). Wing: a crop of the archived whole-car runs;","+  only the change is claimed (the flap tips the air up by about 13° and 8° on the two grids; the angles themselves depend","+  on the box). Splitter: display only. Its face samples sit ahead of the retracted lip, and the short 2-D tunnel (body","+  through the outlet, ~25 % blockage, inlet fixing ρ and u) has a floating pressure level and a slowly filling underbody","+  channel; a load sign needs a velocity inlet with free density, a pressure outlet, a sponge, a finite section whose flows","+  rejoin, and force summed on the wetted faces (open). Corners: still tyres 48 mm above the road. W 196 R: the claim is the","+  wake behind the bare tyre; the streamliner's body fills that patch, and the air beside the car does not settle (the","+  enclosed body runs out through the outlet). Evo arch: one state, a path of the mean flow, not attributed to the flare."," - Not added from docs/research.md: the Vision R 320 CDI (its exhibition has ended) and the Vision Mercedes-Maybach 6","   (never shown at the museum)."," - The original single-file PoC pages are in git history at commit 468cc29 (`museum-tour-poc/`)."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kunabel/workspace/MercedesExperience/CLAUDE.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"04834da0-68c6-4b37-a753-8113563a35d1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/kunabel/workspace/MercedesExpe