{"parentUuid":"ae6c1bf8-ef94-4736-a355-a694da9effe9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQXN1ENPKeXSto6Bd3ww","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Steps 1–4 are partly done. The final W 196 R and arch numbers, the tests, and the commit, push and redeploy are still to come.\n\n**Done so far:**\n- **Splitter:** I stopped its 2.5 mm runs. The step now shows only how the lip divides the air, with no load claim, in both languages; the run record says no claim is made.\n- **Wing:** the text now claims only the change. Raising the flap tips the air up by about 13°, or 8° on the coarser grid, instead of claiming it reverses from down to up.\n- **Arch:** the line is described as a path of the mean flow, and the outward shift is credited to the car's front corner, not the flare.\n- **Release rule:** a 95 % interval over batches, the same sign on both grids, and a larger-tunnel shift smaller than the effect. It is in `tools/cfd/part.mjs`, and each W 196 R run now averages 5 windows instead of 3.\n- **CLAUDE.md:** updated with the review's conclusions.\n\n**W 196 R on the coarse grid:**\n- **Wake behind the bare tyre:** the air there moves at about 40 % of road speed. This is far from zero and should pass the rule.\n- **Air beside the car:** I can't compare the two bodies here. The streamliner run keeps drifting, so the difference crosses zero. Like the splitter, its body runs straight out through the end of the tunnel. This will be marked unresolved.\n- **One limitation of the geometry:** the streamliner's body fills the space where the bare tyre's wake would be, so the \"enclosed\" case can't be measured there. The wheel step will claim the exposed wake and say the comparison beside the car is unsettled. That is your fallback level, which you said is fine.\n\n**Still running:** the two larger-tunnel runs, then the Evo arch and both W 196 R fine-grid runs, finishing around 02:30. After that I'll fill in the remaining wheel and arch numbers in both languages, run `npm test` and the full `npm run e2e`, and commit and push everything to main, including your own uncommitted work and `research_notes/`. I'll then check that the Pages workflow runs and deploys."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":841,"cache_read_input_tokens":277129,"output_tokens":734,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":17},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":841,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":734,"cache_read_input_tokens":277129,"cache_creation_input_tokens":841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":841},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.4.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.4.content.1","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.6.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.6.content.1","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.10.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.12.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.14.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.19.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.21.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.21.content.1","reason":"prefix_binding