{"parentUuid":"5850cf48-ba3c-4ce8-921f-0ba046a1ad6b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQXNqmdi55DdT7WsUiKs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Roughly another 3 hours, so about 03:30–04:00 tonight, mostly simulation:\n\n| Run | Size | Est. finish |\n|---|---|---|\n| W 196 R exposed, larger tunnel (running) | 2.1 M cells, ~28 min | ~00:55 |\n| W 196 R enclosed, larger tunnel | ~28 min | ~01:25 |\n| Evo arch, 24 mm | ~7 min | ~01:30 |\n| W 196 R exposed, 16 mm | 2.7 M cells, ~43 min | ~02:15 |\n| W 196 R enclosed, 16 mm | ~43 min | ~03:00 |\n| Evo arch, 16 mm | ~36 min | ~03:35 |\n| Export, texts EN/HU, `npm test`, full e2e, commit and push, deploy | ~30 min | ~04:00 |\n\nThese estimates come from the two finished coarse runs: about 9 minutes each for 0.8 M cells, and the solver uses all 10 cores.\n\nTwo ways to finish sooner:\n- **Skip the Evo arch 16 mm run:** saves about 35 minutes. It makes no comparison claim, the reviewer accepted it as a one-state illustration, and the coarse grid already has 5 consistent windows. The arch talk would then cite one grid.\n- **Ship now on the coarse grid:** the W 196 R wheel would be released as \"wake on one grid, not yet confirmed on a second\". That's within your fallback, and done in about 30 minutes. Fine grids could follow in a later commit.\n\nUnless you say otherwise, I'll drop only the arch 16 mm run and finish around 03:00."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":397,"cache_read_input_tokens":278712,"output_tokens":1069,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":502},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":397,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1069,"cache_read_input_tokens":278712,"