{"parentUuid":"c70cb1fe-c431-4efd-b06d-50c3a4072085","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9804825a-082f-45e5-a6f0-b978804c77f4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, Bash, Read, SubagentHandback, WebFetch, WebSearch, Write, Yield, mcp__caveman__caveman_retrieve, mcp__claude-in-chrome__browser_batch, mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_context_mcp, mcp__claude-in-chrome__tabs_create_mcp</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Original request:** \"docs/component-cfd-implementation-proposal.md contains fix proposal. Implement it. Update the dev view when done\".\n     - Evo II: replace the whole-car airflow steps with `wing`, `splitter`, `wheel-arch` (race-aero), then `engine`.\n     - W 196 R: one `wheel` step (enclosed/exposed), then `engine`.\n     - Offline data per part goes in `stops/<slug>/cfd/<part>/`, made by `tools/cfd/part.mjs`.\n     - Also required: component player, EN/HU copy, unit and e2e tests, a payload report against 236,084 B, and a reload of the dev view (localhost:8765 in Chrome).\n   - **Earlier questions (all answered):**\n     - Status: done.\n     - Expert brief: done; I offered to save it as a document, and the user didn't respond.\n     - Devview with the current best CFDs: done. Chrome tabs 1061651922 (Evo, `stop.html?s=190e-evo2&debug`) and 1061651925 (W196R); both were hard-reloaded with cmd+shift+r because of caching.\n     - Whether the front splitter is adjustable like the rear flap: answered. Neither moves while driving. The front spoiler is \"adjustable in two stages in the longitudinal direction\" (Mercedes media article); the rear flap is retractable (evo.co.uk: manually adjustable). I offered to add a clarifying sentence; the user didn't answer.\n   - **Expert review:**