ng ν. The 3-D τ is ≈0.5007 at 24 mm, so the closure does the dissipation.\n   - **2-D splitter domain problem:** the body runs through the outlet (25 % solid blockage), so the pressure level floats and the inlet carries a gradient of about 0.9 q. Absolute cp is unusable, and the underbody channel drifts slowly. The display was switched to speed.\n   - **Release gate:** per grid, batch windows of one flow-through each. One-sample t interval, or Welch contrast, at 95 %. Same sign on both grids, and the larger-tunnel shift must be smaller than the credible effect (the interval end nearest zero).\n   - **W196 geometry:**\n     - The enclosed body has 820 mm half-width behind x=500 and continues to the outlet. The exposed body has 330 mm half-width. Tyre at y=665±75, r=340, cut 48 mm above the road.\n     - The station is x=-700 at hub z=344.\n     - The wake patch (y 560–820, z 100–700) is fluid only in the exposed case; the beside patch (y 880–1400, z 100–700) is common to both.\n   - part-field format, race-aero player and panel API are unchanged from before.\n   - Service worker precaches everything under `stops/`. Deploy is a push to main; `.github/workflows/pages.yml` tests, then deploys. Don't use `[skip ci]`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **tools/cfd/part.mjs** (main CLI). Changes this session:\n     - **Wing export:** keep only paths that cross most of the crop: `.filter(l => l.at(-1)[0] < -3180 - 0.6 * (WING.crop.x[1] - WING.crop.x[0]) && l.every((q, n) => n === 0 || q[0] <= l[n - 1][0] + 5))`.\n     - **Statistics:** replaced `settled`/`change` with:\n       ```js\n       const T975 = [NaN, 12.71, 4.30, 3.18, 2.78, 2.57, 2.45, 2.36, 2.31, 2.26, 2.23];\n       const t975 = df => (df >= 30 ? 1.96 : T975[Math.max(1, Math.floor(df))] ?? 2.1);\n       const svar = a => a.reduce((s, v) => s + (v - mean(a)) ** 2, 0) / (a.length - 1);\n       const span = (d, se, df) => ({ d: r3(d), lo: r3(d - (se ? t975(df) * se : 0)), hi: r3(d + (se ? t975(df) * se : 0)) });\n       const interval = a => span(mean(a), Math.sqrt(svar(a) / a.length), a.length - 1);\n       const contrast = (a, b) => { /* b − a, Welch */ ... };\n       function gate(byGrid, domainShift) { /* sign, credible, domain, released: sign !== 0 && domain != null && domain < credible */ }\n       ```\n     - **Splitter:**\n       - Section reverted to the closed underside: `[..., [x1 - 600, 744], [x1 - 600, SPLIT.lip[0]]]`.\n       - Settle is 3·FT (`steps: n + 3 * FT, settle: 3 * FT`).\n       - `SPLIT.grids: [5]` (display only); the default jobs no longer include in-big.\n       - The face samples carry a comment that they are not a lip load.\n       - Export: quantity \"speed-over-inlet\", range [0, 1.4], value `Math.hypot(run.ui[q], run.uk[q]) / run.U`.\n       - Paths are trimmed to the crop: `inCrop`, with stop z ≤ crop top.\n       - The record gets `rec.claim = \"none: ...\"`; `refRho` was removed.\n       - `GRIDS` env var is supported.\n     - **Corners:**\n       - `CORNER` gains `windows: 5`.\n       - w196 gains `wake: { y: [560, 820], z: [100, 700] }` and `beside: { y: [880, 1400], z: [100, 700] }`.\n       - The cornerSolve loop uses `CORNER.windows`, and `steps` uses `CORNER.windows * win`.\n     - **observe for w196:** returns `{ wake: deficit(P.wake), beside: deficit(P.beside), inner, outer, width }`. The deficit is the mean of `1 + v[0]`, sampled every 10 mm, and is null unless every point is fluid.\n     - **cornerExport:**\n       - `GRIDS` env var; `inCrop` trimming of paths, including the follow path.\n       - Loads `${c}-big-24` runs.\n       - w196: `rec.wake` (one-sample interval on exposed, larger-tunnel shift from exposed-big) and `rec.beside` (Welch contrast exposed − enclosed, shift from the big pair), each with `.gate`; `rec.settled = { wake, beside }`.\n       - evo: `rec.repeat` per grid = interval of the shift.\n       - Band guide only for `c === \"exposed\"`; the station faint line runs from y=0 to 1450.\n       - `rec.preview` w