{"parentUuid":"64336794-d1d5-450a-8058-cfe616ef8c71","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQkSLRuEr6A6XdpnSzqo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013oU5Zc3Z9JAVhX6aEipv8T","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nShow the Evo II and W 196 R airflow one part at a time\n\nThe Evo II's whole-car wind tunnel gives way to three precomputed close-ups\n(wing, splitter, wheel arch) and the W 196 R gets a front-wheel close-up,\nplayed by the new race-aero subsystem from per-part field files made by\ntools/cfd/part.mjs (about 107 kB in all, against 236 kB before).\n\nClaims follow an expert review: a sign is stated only when the 95 %\ninterval over one-flow-through batches lies on one side of zero on both\ngrids and a larger tunnel moves it less than the effect. Wing: only the\nchange the flap makes. Splitter: display only. W 196 R: the wake behind\nthe bare tyre (61 % and 44 % speed loss on the 24 and 16 mm grids); the\nair beside the car did not settle and is not claimed. Evo arch: one grid,\na path of the mean flow.\n\nAlso includes in-progress work on several stops, the crank-twist model,\nreal-part photos, research notes and proposals.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit push origin main 2>&1 | tail -2 && sleep 8 && gh run list --limit 2","description":"Commit, push to main and list the deploy runs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":375,"cache_read_input_tokens":142142,"output_tokens":538,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":375,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":538,"cache_read_input_tokens":142